  body: |
    # Type B invalidity legislation in the cited EC framework

    ## Authored interpretation

    The cited framework identifies Type B legislation by dependence of the invalidity-benefit rate on the length of insurance, in contrast with Type A legislation.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 074080–074082; national legislation, insured periods and the applicable coordination regime remain separate dependencies. The association with Type A records a distinction, not equivalence.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 074080, PDF page 55](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/692421b6367485ea116a55db/dmg-ch-07-part-04.pdf#page=55)
    - [DMG 074081, PDF page 55](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/692421b6367485ea116a55db/dmg-ch-07-part-04.pdf#page=55)
    - [DMG 074082, PDF page 55](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/692421b6367485ea116a55db/dmg-ch-07-part-04.pdf#page=55)

